ok   sanitize_filename drops bidi controls and zero-width characters
ok   sanitize_filename strips leading and trailing dots and spaces
ok   sanitize_filename cuts to 255 bytes on a character boundary
ok   sanitize_filename turns invalid UTF-8 into the fallback
ok   sanitize_filename does not modify its argument
ok   sanitize_type keeps a plain media type, lowercased, without parameters
ok   sanitize_type rejects anything that is not type/subtype
ok   sanitize_type allows 127 bytes and refuses 128
ok   content_disposition for a plain name
ok   content_disposition treats an unknown disposition as attachment
ok   content_disposition percent-encodes non-ASCII per RFC 5987 and falls back to underscores
ok   content_disposition keeps CR, LF, quotes and backslashes out of the header
